WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.900
The read side has two parts.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.034
First, a gate from the validation
kit, which works per policy object:

3
00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:09.643
anything targeted in the
directory that isn't fully ready,

4
00:00:09.643 --> 00:00:12.950
or anything in scope that
was never imported, fails it.

5
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.012
Then the move plan works per setting.

6
00:00:15.012 --> 00:00:18.848
Every setting gets a row and a
disposition: a candidate to move,

7
00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:23.737
a conflict between two policies, something
that belongs in Endpoint security,

8
00:00:23.737 --> 00:00:28.100
something with no catalog equivalent,
or something that stays behind.

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.200
And here's the important part:
the plan decides nothing.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.740
A person decides, and records why.
